{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והאש", :translit "veha'esh", :gloss "and the fire"} {:he "והאש על המזבח", :translit "veha'esh al hamizbei'ach", :gloss "and the fire upon the altar"} {:he "והאש ירדה מן השמים", :translit "veha'esh yardah min hashamayim", :gloss "and the fire descended from heaven"} {:he "והאש תאכלם", :translit "veha'esh tochlam", :gloss "and the fire consumed them"} {:he "מן האש יצאו", :translit "min ha'esh yetzu", :gloss "from the fire they went out"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["והאש על המזבח" "והאש ירדה מן השמים" "והאש תאכלם"]} {:kind :other, :note "Pun: they sinned through fire (הורו הלכה) and were punished through fire (והאש תאכלם)"}], :frame {:text "Rav Yehoshua of Sikhnin said in the name of Rav Levi: Nadav and Avihu died because they ruled halakhah before their master, as stated in Vayikra Rabbah 20:8. They reasoned that even though fire descends from heaven, it is still a mitzvah to bring ordinary fire — a position attributed in Eruvin 63a to a disciple who issues a ruling in the presence of his master. The Ba'al HaTurim links the three occurrences of והאש to show that the heavenly fire (והאש ירדה מן השמים) did not exempt them from bringing ordinary fire, and therefore מן האש יצאו (Leviticus 10:2) — they came out through the very element in which they erred.", :sources ["Vayikra Rabbah 20:8" "Eruvin 63a" "Leviticus 10:2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והאש על המזבח תוקד בו", :translit "veha'esh al hamizbei'ach tokad bo", :gloss "and the fire upon the altar shall burn in it"} {:he "ויעל מלאך ה' בלהב המזבח", :translit "veya'al mal'ach hashem belahav hamizbei'ach", :gloss "and the angel of the LORD ascended in the flame of the altar"} {:he "והנה ששה אנשים וגו' ויעמדו אצל מזבח הנחושת", :translit "vehineh shishah anashim vegomer veye'amdu etzel mizbei'ach hanechoshet", :gloss "and behold six men etc. and they stood beside the bronze altar"} {:he "נחשת קלל", :translit "nechoshet kalal", :gloss "kalal bronze"} {:he "ידיו גלילי זהב", :translit "yadav gelilei zahav", :gloss "his hands are rods of gold"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast of materials: outer altar = bronze (מזבח הנחושת / נחשת קלל), inner altar = gold (ידיו גלילי זהב)"}], :frame {:text "Judges 6:21 describes the angel of the LORD ascending in the flame of the altar (ויעל מלאך ה' בלהב המזבח). Ezekiel 9:2 describes six men standing beside the bronze altar (ויעמדו אצל מזבח הנחושת). Ezekiel 1:7 describes the divine beings' feet as sparkling like the appearance of kalal bronze (כעין נחשת קלל). The golden altar is described in Exodus 30:3. Ezekiel 1:7 describes the feet of the living creatures as gleaming like burnished bronze (כעין נחשת קלל). The verse Song of Songs 5:14 describes hands as rods of gold (ידיו גלילי זהב). The rule that a sin-offering whose blood was brought inside the sanctuary is not eaten is stated at Mishnah Zevachim 10:7 and discussed in Talmud Zevachim 56a. The outer altar's bronze links it to the angelic realm; the inner altar's gold links it to the Shekhinah, and therefore eating does not apply above.", :sources ["Judges 6:21" "Ezekiel 9:2" "Ezekiel 1:7" "Exodus 30:3" "Song of Songs 5:14" "Mishnah Zevachim 10:7" "Zevachim 56a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["והאש על המזבח" "והאש ירדה מן השמים" "והאש תאכלם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "והאש על המזבח", :refs ["Leviticus 6:5"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "והאש ירדה מן השמים", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "והאש תאכלם", :refs ["Ezekiel 15:7"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Pun: they sinned through fire (הורו הלכה) and were punished through fire (והאש תאכלם)", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Contrast of materials: outer altar = bronze (מזבח הנחושת / נחשת קלל), inner altar = gold (ידיו גלילי זהב)", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:24.948714820Z", :model "glm-5.2"}